  "details": "w_2021.1.5p3-feb41055d1\nHere's a short sample of a 1000hz sine wave transmitted to a listener. I'm displaying the audio using Audacity, zoomed into a ~0.08 second section of audio. I'm also using a plugin to measure peak amplitude in a selected duration. ONSP is on the top, noise on the bottom. This was recorded in the VRChat Home, with the listener and sender sitting in the same spot for each recording.\n\nAs you can see, noise's audio is significantly quieter! It should be tuned to match ONSP. If a user wants to turn voice down generally, they should do so using the app's volume controls.",
